{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7A9qmzqS1VfmuqoWL6y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"contract_version\":\"agent3-advisor-draft-v11\",\"summary\":null,\"summary_sentences\":[{\"text\":\"Three tutors report audio playback that stops or stalls after seeking, scrubbing or jumping back, on AUD-741, AUD-754 and AUD-768.\",\"support_claim_ids\":[\"c1\",\"c2\",\"c3\"]},{\"text\":\"Current triage guidance says to collect task IDs, browser versions and reproduction steps and send one scoped engineering incident; no cause is confirmed.\",\"support_claim_ids\":[\"c7\"],\"depends_on\":[1]}],\"detail_sentences\":[{\"text\":\"A tutor reports on AUD-741 (Firefox 132.0.2) that the sound stops after dragging the waveform back to the start, with the time display at 0:00; reopening restores it until the next seek.\",\"support_claim_ids\":[\"c1\"]},{\"text\":\"A tutor reports on AUD-754 (Chrome 131.0.6778.85) that the clock never advances after moving the scrubber, and a QA tutor reports reproducing the stuck clock on that task and that the downloaded WAV plays normally.\",\"support_claim_ids\":[\"c2\",\"c4\"]},{\"text\":\"A tutor reports an endless spinner after jump-back on AUD-768 (Firefox 132.0.2), after playback had already worked.\",\"support_claim_ids\":[\"c3\"]},{\"text\":\"In the AUD-741 thread a QA tutor asked for the task ID and browser build and said a second reproduction is needed before filing; the tutor then supplied both.\",\"support_claim_ids\":[\"c5\"]},{\"text\":\"In the AUD-768 thread the team lead asked the thread starter to keep the affected task open and add browser and task details to one report.\",\"support_claim_ids\":[\"c6\"]}],\"reasoning\":\"Three tutors in separate threads report playback failing after seeking, on different tasks and two browsers. Task IDs and browsers are available for all three and a QA tutor reproduced one, which meets the guidance's collection step. The guidance supports one scoped engineering incident. The media-input FAQ does not apply, since the player clock is stuck, not advancing normally.\",\"claims\":[{\"claim_id\":\"c1\",\"kind\":\"INCIDENT_FACT\",\"text\":\"A tutor reports that on AUD-741 in Firefox 132.0.2 the sound stops after dragging the waveform back to the start with the time display at 0:00, that it played the first time, and that reopening restores it until they seek again.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\",\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\"],\"attributions\":[{\"user_id\":\"U9106\",\"relation\":\"AUTHOR\",\"evidence_id\":\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792137900.000000\"},{\"user_id\":\"U9106\",\"relation\":\"AUTHOR\",\"evidence_id\":\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792138140.000000\"}]},{\"claim_id\":\"c2\",\"kind\":\"INCIDENT_FACT\",\"text\":\"A tutor reports that on AUD-754 in Chrome 131.0.6778.85 reloading gives one listen, and after moving the scrubber the play triangle changes but the clock never advances.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139520.000000\"],\"attributions\":[{\"user_id\":\"U9107\",\"relation\":\"AUTHOR\",\"evidence_id\":\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139520.000000\"}]},{\"claim_id\":\"c3\",\"kind\":\"INCIDENT_FACT\",\"text\":\"A tutor reports an endless spinner after using jump-back on AUD-768 in Firefox 132.0.2, after playback had already worked.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792141440.000000\"],\"attributions\":[{\"user_id\":\"U9108\",\"relation\":\"AUTHOR\",\"evidence_id\":\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792141440.000000\"}]},{\"claim_id\":\"c4\",\"kind\":\"INCIDENT_FACT\",\"text\":\"A QA tutor reports reproducing the stuck clock on AUD-754 and says the downloaded WAV plays normally.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139640.000000\"],\"attributions\":[{\"user_id\":\"U9104\",\"relation\":\"AUTHOR\",\"evidence_id\":\"m:C_91AUDIO01:1792139640.000000\"}]},{\"claim_id\":\"c5\",\"kind\":\"INCIDENT_FACT\",\"text\":\"A QA tutor asks the thread starter for the task ID and browser build, saying a second reproduction is needed b